Expand the vector product as a determinant:

$$\mathbf{a}\times\mathbf{b} = \begin{vmatrix}\mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k}\\ x & -1 & 3\\ 1 & 1 & -2y\end{vmatrix}
= \mathbf{i}\big[(-1)(-2y) - 3\cdot 1\big] - \mathbf{j}\big[x(-2y) - 3\cdot 1\big] + \mathbf{k}\big[x\cdot 1 - (-1)\cdot 1\big]$$

$$\mathbf{a}\times\mathbf{b} = (2y - 3)\mathbf{i} + (2xy + 3)\mathbf{j} + (x + 1)\mathbf{k}.$$

Equate with $-\mathbf{i} + 7\mathbf{j} + 3\mathbf{k}$ component by component:

- $\mathbf{i}$: $2y - 3 = -1$, so $y = 1$;
- $\mathbf{k}$: $x + 1 = 3$, so $x = 2$;
- $\mathbf{j}$ (check): $2xy + 3 = 2(2)(1) + 3 = 7$. This agrees with the given value.

$$\boxed{x = 2,\quad y = 1}$$

(These are integers, as required by $x, y \in \mathbb{Z}$.)
